    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0337" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.20/6–548</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Latin American Branch, General Staff,
                        United States Army</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Freeman</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of
                        Plans and Operations, General Staff, United States Army</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wedemeyer</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d231-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-04">4 June 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>At a conference with the Secretary of the Army on 21 May 1948, the
                        Argentine Minister of War presented a memorandum which stated in substance: <list>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The Argentines appreciated the offer of the surplus property which
                                was indicated to be available in the interim replies of March and
                                May 1948 and which had been requested in List 1 of the
                                Critten-berger Memorandum of 8 December 1947.<anchor n="2"
                                    xml:id="d231-f2"/>
                            </item>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                            <item> The Argentines had reduced their request for complete
                                organizational units of equipment and now desired to procure
                                complete units of organizational equipment for only: <list>
                                    <item>1 self-propelled 40mm antiaircraft battery;</item>
                                    <item>1 company of medium tanks;</item>
                                    <item>1 company of light tanks;</item>
                                    <item>1 reconnaissance troop of the armored division;</item>
                                    <item>1 headquarters and service troop of the armored
                                        division;</item>
                                    <item>1 battery of self-propelled 105mm howitzers.</item>
                                </list> All of the foregoing equipment was to be in accordance with
                                the latest United States tables of organization and equipment. </item>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</label>
                            <item>Assistance was also requested from the United States Army in the
                                procurement from commercial sources of additional military
                                equipment.</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>To provide the Argentine Government with the six organizational units set
                        forth above, the President was requested to authorize the sale of this
                        matériel under Public Resolution No. 83 of 1940. At noon on 3 June 1948, the
                        President authorized the Secretary of the Army to make the sale. ...</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. L. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Freeman, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, GSC</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d231-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d231-f1-content">
                <p>This document, along with the letter by Royall (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>), was forwarded by Freeman to John C. Dreier, Chief of the
                    Division of Special Inter-American Affairs in a memorandum dated June 5, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
